00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:51.800
Cloud.

00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:54.890
Here's another example of where
we track API response time.

00:26:54.890 --> 00:26:55.807
So this is a similar--

00:26:55.807 --> 00:26:58.181
you know, this is an application
level metric, not really

00:26:58.181 --> 00:26:59.070
system level metric.

00:26:59.070 --> 00:27:02.880
But we're tracking just
response times and capabilities.

00:27:02.880 --> 00:27:06.410
So this was actually a new
endpoint in our storage system

00:27:06.410 --> 00:27:08.774
that we have been developing
for some new capabilities

00:27:08.774 --> 00:27:10.190
that our developers
wanted to use.

00:27:10.190 --> 00:27:12.050
And we're tracking it
sort of over history.

00:27:12.050 --> 00:27:14.792
But you'll see that we can
tell when we flip the switch,

00:27:14.792 --> 00:27:16.250
when that started
